# PageShell

- Use `PageShell` for route-entry page layout in `src/features`; keep `src/app/**/page.tsx` thin.
- Use `PageContainer` as a low-level primitive for inner width caps and gutters inside sections or special layouts.
- Prefer `preset` as the main API for `PageShell`: `form | content | wide | full`.
- Tailwind width classes stay internal to `src/ui/page-shell.tsx`; do not expose `max-w-*` semantics in page code.
- Use overrides only when needed: `width` for exceptions, `spacing` for page-level vertical rhythm, `inset` for gutter control.
- Do not model sidebar/account/management pages as another `PageShell` preset. Create a separate structural shell such as `SidebarPageShell`.

## Preset Guide

- `form`: login, signup, narrow step flows.
- `content`: profile pages, medium-width readable content.
- `wide`: broader standard pages without sidebar.
- `full`: full-bleed outer shell; inner sections may still use `PageContainer`.

## Examples

```tsx
// auth or narrow flow page
<PageShell preset="form">...</PageShell>

// medium-width content page
<PageShell preset="content">...</PageShell>

// wide standard page
<PageShell preset="wide" spacing="md">...</PageShell>

// full-bleed page shell with capped inner section
<PageShell preset="full">
  <section>
    <PageContainer width="desktop">...</PageContainer>
  </section>
</PageShell>
```

## Override Heuristics

- Use `width="compact"` only for intentional narrower-than-preset pages.
- Use `spacing="none"` for loaders, splash states, or full-height placeholders.
- Use `inset="none"` only when the page or section fully owns its own horizontal gutters.
